* {{hyph|en|equip}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|equips|equipping|equipped|equipped|past_ptc2=equipt}} (''equipt'' is archaic)

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[furnish]] for [[service]], or against a [[need]] or [[exigency]]; to fit out; to supply with whatever is necessary to efficient action in any way; to provide with arms or an armament, stores, munitions, rigging, etc.; -- said especially of ships and of troops.
#* {{rfquotek|en|Dryden}}.
#: ''Gave orders for '''equipping''' a considerable fleet.'' {{rfdatek|en|Ludlow}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[dress up]]; to [[array]]; [[accouter]].
#* {{RQ:Spectator|2|129|2 July 1711}}
#*: The country are led astray in following the town, and '''equipped''' in a ridiculous habit, when they fancy themselves in the height of the mode.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To prepare (someone) with a skill

